				(color 200 0 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "cbf53565-9a79-53b6-96c1-077b851be609")
	)
	(text "K1 is an Omron G6S-2F (SMD, both poles in parallel); R3/C8 delay its make so K_XFER is\nback on NC first (interlock margin 6.1 ms, simulated). F1, an on-board NANO2 2 A slow-blow\nfuse in a clip, replaces J3 and the in-line fuse. F2 + R12 replace the fusible NFR25. R9 is\na four-terminal Kelvin shunt (sense on pins 2 and 3). C1 is 470 uF (was 4700 uF).\nPart and Digi-Key numbers: polarization_switch_rev_D_BOM.xlsx."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -4140.454 2226.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d5e548d2-caca-5f70-b848-70c22bbc66be")
	)
	(text "SEQUENCE (fixed delays, never timed on I_SENSE)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -4139.438 2147.624 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(thickness 0.36)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e9658903-49b6-5db8-82c6-2fc52f35faca")
	)
	(text "DRAIN reaches ~222 V at switch-off and COIL_N swings from +223 V to -154 V (D5 holds up\nto ~347 V between them). DRAIN, COIL_N and SNUB are in net class HV; keep XFER >= 1.25 mm\nfrom all three."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -4139.438 2166.5 0)
